research/audit/wave0-judge-adjudications.jsonl-61-{"id":"lem-rat-cut-embeds","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"6583dc1e97236adc8d59d59e8b663a90bf8215c733d05b2404548a2a93e35841","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"other","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5, high reasoning effort)","at":"2026-08-02","round":2,"note":"CONFIRMED FATAL and repaired. Round-2 rejection on the text I repaired at A8 round 1 — and it EXPOSED rather than introduced the defect: the title and step 4.1 are untouched by my [L5] repair, and DeepSeek simply moved to the next defect once the false cut-product domain was gone. Verified from disk: the title read 'The rational cuts embed densely as an ordered SUBFIELD' and step 4.1 concluded 'a dense embedding of ORDERED FIELDS', while the Statement establishes only injectivity, order preservation and reflection, the four ring identities and density. Closure of the image under reciprocals — which 'subfield' requires — is nowhere proved, and cannot be proved here without knowing R is a field, which thm-reals-dedekind-field establishes USING this lemma. So the title asserted something the item not only does not prove but cannot prove in place. Title asserting more than the proof gives is fatal-class in the step-6 charter and judges cannot see titles. Repair: retitled to 'The rational cuts embed densely in R, preserving sums, products, 0, 1 and the order', matching the Statement clause for clause; step 4.1's conclusion narrowed to 'a dense, order-preserving ring embedding of Q into R' (the Statement's own phrase) with an explicit note that closure under reciprocals is not established here. I deliberately did NOT wikilink thm-reals-dedekind-field in that note: it cites this lemma, so the link would be circular."}
research/audit/wave0-judge-adjudications.jsonl-62-{"id":"lem-rat-cut-embeds","model":"claude-sonnet-5","context_sha256":"6583dc1e97236adc8d59d59e8b663a90bf8215c733d05b2404548a2a93e35841","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5, high reasoning effort)","at":"2026-08-02","round":2,"note":"UPHELD in substance and repaired, though graded nonfatal rather than fatal. Sonnet is right that [L6] attributed commutativity, associativity, distributivity AND the strict midpoint property to thm-rat-ordered-field, and that thm-rat-field was absent from deps. Two reasons this is not the fatal class I applied to thm-reals-dedekind-field [L7]: (i) thm-rat-ordered-field's Statement itself reads 'makes the FIELD Q ([[thm-rat-field]]) a totally ordered field', so it asserts the field structure and links its source — the reader reaches the ring axioms in one hop, unlike [L7] of thm-reals-dedekind-field, which cited the order-free thm-rat-field for an order property and left the reader at a dead end; (ii) the midpoint property is true and three lines from the cited axioms. This is the same shape as the lem-rat-triangle rejection I ruled a false positive in round 1, and I have kept that ruling for the same reason. Repaired anyway because the item was already being reopened for the DeepSeek fatal, so the marginal cost was nil and a third rejection was foreseeable: [L6] now attributes the field axioms to thm-rat-field (added to deps, with an exact citation contract), the three order axioms verbatim to thm-rat-ordered-field, and marks order-scaling and the midpoint as the CONSEQUENCES they are, with the one-line reason (2 = 1 + 1 > 0 is invertible and 2r < r + s < 2s)."}
