research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/cex-limsup-infinite-not-attained-in-r.md-3220-[L10] Archimedean facts: for every real $M$ there is a natural $p \ge 1$ with $M < p \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$, and for every real $\eta > 0$ a natural $m \ge 1$ with $1/m < \eta$; the canonical naturals satisfy $0 \le n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$ and are increasing in $n$, and $0 < a \le b$ gives $0 < 1/b \le 1/a$ ([[thm-of-archimedean]], [[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]], [[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]]).
