research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md-2721-[L2] Monotonicity of the tail bounds: $s_m \le s_n$ and $i_n \le i_m$ whenever $n \le m$, and $i_n \le s_n$ for every $n$; both $\limsup_k x_k = \inf\{s_n\}$ and $\liminf_k x_k = \sup\{i_n\}$ exist ([[lem-limsup-exists]], [[def-limsup-liminf]]).
