research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md-2826-[L4] Absolute value: $|u| < c$ if and only if $-c < u < c$, for $c > 0$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md-2827-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md-2828-[L5] Order arithmetic in $\mathbb{R}$: adding a constant preserves $<$ and $\le$; $u \le v$ and $v < w$ give $u < w$; trichotomy, so exactly one of $z < 0$, $z = 0$, $z > 0$ holds and the negation of $z < 0$ is $z \ge 0$; $u \le v$ if and only if $v - u \ge 0$; and $u < u$ is impossible ([[lem-of-add-order]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]], [[def-ordered-field]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md-2829-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md:2830:[L6] The order on $\mathbb{N}$ is total, so any two indices admit a common upper bound ([[thm-nat-linear-order]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md-2831-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md-2832-[L7] For $c \in \mathbb{R}$ the constant sequence $(c)$ converges to $c$ ([[def-sequence]], [[def-real-limit]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md-2833-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-limsup-is-greatest-subsequential-limit.md-2834-[L8] A sequence of reals has at most one limit ([[lem-limit-unique]]), which is what licenses writing $\lim_k x_k$ and $\lim_k y_k$ for the limits named in the statement; without it those symbols would not denote.
