research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-3172-[L2] Rational powers: $x^{1/n}$ is the rational power at exponent $1/n$; for rational $t > 0$, $x > 1$ implies $x^t > 1$; and $(xy)^{1/n} = x^{1/n} y^{1/n}$ for $x, y > 0$ ([[def-rational-power]], [[lem-rational-power-monotone]], [[lem-rational-power-laws]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-3173-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-3174-[L3] Bernoulli's inequality: $(1+x)^n \ge 1 + \iota(n) x$ for $x \ge -1$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}$ ([[lem-bernoulli-inequality]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-3175-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md:3176:[L4] Canonical naturals: $\iota(n) > 0$ and invertible for $n \ge 1$, and $\iota$ is strictly increasing ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[def-nat-order]], [[thm-nat-linear-order]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-3177-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-3178-[L5] Reciprocal Archimedean property: for every real $\eta > 0$ there is a natural $p \ge 1$ with $1/p < \eta$; and $0 < x < y$ gives $0 < 1/y < 1/x$ ([[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]], [[thm-of-archimedean]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-3179-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-3180-[L6] Order arithmetic: inequalities may be added and translated, and multiplying an inequality by a positive element preserves it; the order is total, so exactly one of $a < 1$, $a = 1$, $a > 1$ holds ([[lem-of-add-order]], [[lem-of-sign-rules]], [[def-ordered-field]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]]).
