research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-4171-[L6] Convergence to a real $L$ means: for every rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $K$ with $|x_k - L| < \varepsilon$ for all $k \ge K$; and the same relation is obtained by testing every real $\varepsilon > 0$ instead, since below any positive real lies a positive rational ([[def-real-limit]], [[def-sequence]], [[lem-rat-embeds-dense]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-4172-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-4173-[L7] Divergence: $x_k \to +\infty$ means that for every real $M$ there is $K$ with $x_k > M$ for all $k \ge K$ ([[def-divergence-to-infinity]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-4174-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md:4175:[L8] Eventually and frequently, and the fact that a property holding eventually holds frequently, since indices beyond any two given thresholds exist by totality of the order on $\mathbb{N}$; likewise two properties each holding eventually hold together from the larger threshold on ([[def-sequence]], [[thm-nat-linear-order]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-4176-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-4177-[L9] Absolute value: for $c > 0$, $|a| < c$ if and only if $-c < a < c$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-4178-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/thm-ratio-root-inequality.md-4179-[L10] Order arithmetic in $\mathbb{R}$: $0 < 1$, so $t < t + 1$ for every real $t$, and no real is above every real; adding a constant preserves the order ([[cor-of-one-positive]], [[lem-of-add-order]], [[def-ordered-field]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]]).
