research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/rem-extended-real-conventions.md-282-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/rem-extended-real-conventions.md-283-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/rem-extended-real-conventions.md-284-**Given:** The canonical naturals $\iota(n) = n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$; the sequence $x_k := 1/\iota(k+1)$; for a real $c > 0$ the sequence $y^{(c)}_k := c\,\iota(k+1)$; and the sequence $z_k := \iota(k+1)\,\iota(k+1)$.
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/rem-extended-real-conventions.md-285-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/rem-extended-real-conventions.md:286:[L1] Canonical naturals: $\iota(n) > 0$ and invertible for $n \ge 1$, $\iota$ is strictly increasing, and $\iota(n) \ge 1$ for $n \ge 1$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[def-nat-order]], [[thm-nat-linear-order]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/rem-extended-real-conventions.md-287-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/rem-extended-real-conventions.md-288-[L2] Archimedean facts: for every real $\eta > 0$ there is a natural $p \ge 1$ with $1/p < \eta$, and for every real $M$ there is a natural $p \ge 1$ with $M < \iota(p)$; and $0 < u < v$ gives $0 < 1/v < 1/u$ ([[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]], [[thm-of-archimedean]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]]).
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/rem-extended-real-conventions.md-289-
research/audit/wave6-refuter-tasks/rem-extended-real-conventions.md-290-[L3] Convergence to a real and divergence to $+\infty$; to establish convergence it suffices to produce a threshold for every real $\varepsilon > 0$; a constant sequence converges to its value ([[def-real-limit]], [[def-sequence]], [[def-divergence-to-infinity]]).
