research/audit/wave5-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-051-lem-cauchy-with-convergent-subsequence.prompt.md-164-[L3] Halving a rational: if $\varepsilon$ is a positive rational then so is $\varepsilon/2$, and the embedding of $\mathbb{Q}$ in $\mathbb{R}$ is a field embedding, so the image of $\varepsilon/2$ is half the image of $\varepsilon$ and the two halves sum to $\varepsilon$ ([[lem-rat-embeds-dense]]).
