research/audit/wave5-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-051-lem-cauchy-with-convergent-subsequence.prompt.md-168-[L5] Convergence: $(x_k)$ converges to $L$ when for every rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $K$ with $|x_k - L| < \varepsilon$ for all $k \ge K$ ([[def-real-limit]]).
