research/audit/wave5-dispatch/audit-alpha-a6-round3.result.json:16:  "tail": "**A6 is clear — 14/14 gates.** The round-3 blocker is closed.\n\n**`risk_review`: 131/131 complete** (was 0/131 after two rounds). The ordering fix the dispatch asked for worked: records first.\n\n- I read **all 100 items** that had no returning refuter lane — in full, from disk: Statement, Facts, every numbered step against the facts it cites, and Remarks read with a numbered step's suspicion. Several cores I re-derived rather than read (the cardinal-supremum argument in `lem-character-is-well-defined`, the Δ-system induction, the subtracted-closure construction in `thm-perfectly-normal-implies-completely-normal`, the whole K-topology non-regularity chain, the three-topology comparison bound).\n- Notes are per-item and state which lane actually backs each one. I **rewrote two boilerplate sentences in the inherited generator before using it** — they claimed every `[L#]` fact had been checked against its dependency page on disk, and that Alpha had verified every cross-reference a tool-less lane couldn't. Neither was true as a blanket claim. Each `alpha-read` note now also says plainly that it is single-reader, same-family evidence, and that the tier is a heuristic score, not a finding.\n\n**11 nonfatal findings recorded, none repaired** (this round licenses no mathematical edit). The two most substantive: `thm-cantor-cubes-are-ccc` applies the Δ-system lemma to the cylinder supports without first showing that family is uncountable (closes in one line via a finite-to-one count); `lem-compact-closed-balls-...` binds `r` as arbitrary at step 1.2 and silently rebinds the same letter at 2.3. The rest are misdirected citations, a wrong internal step pointer, and two unhandled trivial cases.\n\nPositional claims I checked rather than assumed, since round 2 found a false one — all six resolved correctly against the page manifest and disk.\n\n**genrisk: 3/3 seeds dispositioned** `verified-generated`. All three have empty logical cones, so retag/restate/unfold are each wrong for a stated reason. On `ex-contractive-sequence-fixed-point` I checked the Remark arithmetic, which is where an invented example fails: the cited error bound evaluates to exactly `|1/2 − x_k|`, so it holds with equality and is not overstated.\n\nTwo things worth your attention:\n\n- **The merged contract file is a trap.** `wave5-proof-contracts.json` was stale against the batch files and reported six spurious `risk-review-missing` errors until re-merged. It's a build product; it must be regenerated after any batch write.\n- **The refuter runner still has no retry.** Lanes keep dying with `TypeError: terminated` — null results, never verdicts. I relaunched the fleet in the background (it raised coverage 31→48 while I read, and is still running), but it gated nothing. Re-running the generator later would upgrade more notes from `alpha-read` to `refuter-read` without invalidating anything written.\n\nRound 3 is appended to `research/audit/wave5-alpha.md`. No item file was touched, and no `verification.judge` was written. Next action is A7."
