research/audit/wave6-real-analysis-laurent.findings.md-46-
research/audit/wave6-real-analysis-laurent.findings.md-47-> [L5] An ordered field is a field with a subset $P$ satisfying (O1) trichotomy, for each $x$ exactly one of $x \in P$, $x = 0$, $-x \in P$, and (O2) closure of $P$ under addition and multiplication; the order is then $a < b :\iff b - a \in P$ ([[def-ordered-field]]). For $n \ge 1$, $n \cdot 1_F$ is the $n$-fold sum of $1_F$, and $0 \cdot 1_F = 0$ ([[def-archimedean-field]]).
